       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** The usual prescription limit is 3,200 mg/day. That's typically 800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. Single doses above 800 mg aren't standard.\n- **Risk:** At 6,400 mg/day, the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum anti-inflammatory dose.\n2. **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 400 mg PO every 6 hours for a lower-intensity regimen.\n3. **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily.\n4. **Something else.** If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the rationale. I'd enter it with a note, but I'd want that confirmation first.\n\nOnce you pick one, I'll enter it right away. If you have a preferred indication or duration, I can add it to the order note."
