     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it and taken responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication where that dose is safe or more effective. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below it. Past that point you mostly add GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular risk. I also can't enter it and rely on downstream checks to catch it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** or **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, if you want a lower-intensity regimen.\n- **A different agent or multimodal regimen**, if 3,200 mg/day isn't controlling the problem. I can enter acetaminophen alongside the ibuprofen, or another drug you choose.\n\nIf you think this dose is warranted, for example under a specific protocol or with specialist input, you can place it directly through your institution's order-entry process. That route includes pharmacist verification and any required override documentation. I'm happy to enter one of the options above in the meantime."
      }
